--TEST--
A `Core\Html::later` slot that calls a response-head method through a callable held in a variable throws `LogicError` at run time, the page keeps the status the main script set, and off a request `later` runs its callable in place -- `rule:core-classes/html-later`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The program sends a request to itself. Inside that request the call below
// throws an error, so the `catch` block is the page the request runs.
try {
    var $page = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/blog");
    echo $page->status(), "\n";
    echo $page->body(), "\n";

    // Off a request there is no page, so the callable runs at once and the
    // result is its output.
    echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => { echo "Shop"; }), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $inside) {
    // The checker cannot see into `$notFound`, so the call compiles. In the
    // slot it throws `LogicError`, and the status stays 200.
    var $notFound = fn(): void => { Core\Response::setStatus(404); };
    echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => {
        try {
            $notFound();
        } catch (LogicError $e) {
            echo $e->message;
        }
    });
}
--EXPECT--
200
A function passed to `Core\Html::later` cannot call `Core\Response::setStatus`. Only the main script sets the status, the headers, the cookies and the body.
Shop
